00:54:38.630 --> 00:54:47.530
that I would have put into a script because it did not feel like a very noble Jim, successful
因为那感觉不像是一个高尚的吉姆，一个成功的

1479
00:54:47.530 --> 00:54:50.550
social guy moment.
社交达人会有的时刻。

1480
00:54:50.550 --> 00:54:55.990
It felt really like people are going to hate him for this or disrespect him or whatever.
我当时觉得大家会因为这件事讨厌他，或者看不起他之类的。

1481
00:54:55.990 --> 00:54:59.530
So I kind of felt it was risky to put it out there.
所以我总觉得把它放出来很有风险。

1482
00:55:00.950 --> 00:55:01.550
I don't know.
我不知道。

1483
00:55:01.610 --> 00:55:05.530
It was very hard also in the edit to keep it that long.
在剪辑的时候，要保持那么长的时长也很困难。

1484
00:55:05.910 --> 00:55:10.890
I mean, we tried to make the same length that you guys really did in the scene.
我的意思是，我们试着保持你们在现场拍的那种长度。

1485
00:55:11.130 --> 00:55:13.770
And there was a lot of urge to like trim that up.
当时确实很想把它剪短一点。

1486
00:55:13.850 --> 00:55:16.610
That's an awful long time to have people not talk.
让人们在那儿沉默那么久，时间太长了。

1487
00:55:16.610 --> 00:55:18.690
Yes, let's talk about that.
没错，我们来聊聊那个。

1488
00:55:18.890 --> 00:55:19.470
It's so beautiful.
那太美了。

1489
00:55:19.770 --> 00:55:20.530
It's so beautiful.
那太美了。

1490
00:55:20.910 --> 00:55:26.370
Pam and Jim are on the deck of that boat and Pam does give him an opening.
帕姆和吉姆在船的甲板上，帕姆确实给了他一个机会。

1491
00:55:26.810 --> 00:55:28.990
She says, sometimes I just don't get Roy.
她说，有时候我就是搞不懂罗伊。

1492
00:55:29.610 --> 00:55:37.730
And this is the first time we've seen her complain about Roy to Jim to disparage her relationship.
这是我们第一次看到她向吉姆抱怨罗伊，贬低她自己的这段关系。

1493
00:55:38.770 --> 00:55:41.390
Really, it's the first time she's verbalized it.
真的，这是她第一次把它说出口。

1494
00:55:41.530 --> 00:55:42.670
I don't, I'm pretty sure.
我不确定，但我很肯定。

1495
00:55:42.670 --> 00:55:46.350
And then it is 27 seconds of silence.
然后就是长达27秒的沉默。

1496
00:55:46.950 --> 00:55:54.010
And a fan wrote in, Anthony Sneed said, what was the motivation behind that awkward silence?
有位粉丝安东尼·斯尼德写信问，那段尴尬沉默背后的动机是什么？

1497
00:55:54.370 --> 00:55:56.410
There's a lot going on in those 27 seconds.
在那27秒里，发生了很多事。

1498
00:55:56.490 --> 00:55:59.010
Just because people aren't talking doesn't mean nothing's going on.
仅仅因为人们没在说话，并不代表什么都没发生。

1499
00:55:59.110 --> 00:56:04.770
And I think that you look at his face and, you know, you can see him trying out different
我觉得你看着他的脸，你知道，你能看到他在尝试各种

1500
00:56:04.770 --> 00:56:10.910
things and thinking and being, you know, urged to go forward and blocked and, you know,
想法，在思考，你知道，那种想要前进却又受阻的冲动，你知道，

1501
00:56:10.910 --> 00:56:18.350
and, and then I think also on your face, there's all this kind of like disappointment that he's
还有，我觉得你脸上也写满了那种失望，因为他

1502
00:56:18.350 --> 00:56:23.790
not going to do anything and face saving when you're like, well, I'm cold and kind of, it
什么都不会做，而当你表现得像是在说“我冷”的时候，其实也是在给自己找台阶下，

1503
00:56:23.790 --> 00:56:25.350
was kind of good that it was cold actually.
而且说实话，天冷其实挺好的。

1504
00:56:25.970 --> 00:56:30.410
And we really did shoot it out in the Harbor because I think you wouldn't have been able
我们确实是在港口实景拍摄的，因为我觉得如果你不在那儿，

1505
00:56:30.410 --> 00:56:33.110
to like, your, your nose was red.
你的鼻子就不会冻红了。

1506
00:56:33.230 --> 00:56:33.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1507
00:56:34.030 --> 00:56:34.930
I was cold.
我是真的很冷。

1508
00:56:35.110 --> 00:56:35.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1509
00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:35.850
You were cold.
你确实很冷。

1510
00:56:36.170 --> 00:56:36.410
Yeah.
没错。

1511
00:56:36.510 --> 00:56:37.130
I believed it.
我当时就信了。

1512
00:56:37.130 --> 00:56:40.170
Now, Greg, it wasn't in the script that there would be a big pause.
格雷格，剧本里可没写这里要有一个大停顿。

1513
00:56:40.970 --> 00:56:44.810
It didn't say there's a long, big pause.
上面没说要有一个漫长的大停顿。

1514
00:56:45.050 --> 00:56:45.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1515
00:56:45.370 --> 00:56:48.970
It just says that they look at each other and then finally Pam says.
上面只写了他们互相对视，然后帕姆终于开口说话了。

1516
00:56:49.590 --> 00:56:49.810
Yeah.
没错。

1517
00:56:50.310 --> 00:56:57.170
And, but I remember on the day you really encouraging us to take our time and don't be afraid to
但我记得拍摄那天，你确实鼓励我们慢慢来，不要害怕

1518
00:56:57.170 --> 00:56:58.470
just look at each other.
只是看着对方。

1519
00:56:59.150 --> 00:57:06.450
Well, I mean, that was part of, I think what made the show so special was that, and so different
嗯，我是说，我觉得这正是这部剧如此特别的原因，也让它与

1520
00:57:06.450 --> 00:57:13.250
from what was on TV, you know, was that moments of behavior were really important more so than
当时电视上的其他节目截然不同，你知道，行为本身的瞬间比

1521
00:57:13.250 --> 00:57:15.910
jokes and setups and punchlines and lines and stuff.
笑话、铺垫、包袱和台词之类的东西要重要得多。

1522
00:57:15.910 --> 00:57:23.850
And so, and I think that came out of appreciating what's good about a documentary and documentaries
所以，我觉得这源于对纪录片优点的欣赏，而纪录片

1523
00:57:23.850 --> 00:57:30.950
just are all about finding the truth in what people are doing and leaning in and no matter
的核心就在于发现人们行为背后的真相，并深入挖掘，无论

1524
00:57:30.950 --> 00:57:34.890
what they think they're doing or what they say they're doing, what are they, what are their
他们自认为在做什么，或者嘴上说在做什么，他们的

1525
00:57:34.890 --> 00:57:36.330
actions show you that they're doing?
行动向你展示了他们在做什么？

1526
00:57:36.750 --> 00:57:42.430
And this was like a good romantic example of, you know, it all being in between the lines
这就像是一个浪漫的好例子，你知道，一切都在字里行间，

1527
00:57:42.430 --> 00:57:45.270
and it all being on the faces and not in the script.
一切都在脸上，而不是在剧本里。

1528
00:57:46.130 --> 00:57:46.210
So.
所以。

1529
00:57:46.410 --> 00:57:47.790
That is so smartly said.
说得太精辟了。

1530
00:57:47.930 --> 00:57:51.870
You guys, should we talk about what else was going on during this scene?
各位，我们要聊聊这场戏拍摄期间还发生了什么吗？

1531
00:57:52.270 --> 00:57:55.290
Do you mean when half of the cast got lost at sea?
你是说有一半演员在海上迷路那次吗？

1532
00:57:55.810 --> 00:57:56.290
Yes.
没错。

1533
00:57:57.750 --> 00:57:58.370
All right.
好吧。

1534
00:57:58.390 --> 00:57:59.450
So here's the deal.
事情是这样的。

1535
00:57:59.670 --> 00:58:02.790
When we started this scene, I think we knew it was going to take a while.
我们开始拍这场戏时，我想我们都知道这会花不少时间。

1536
00:58:03.070 --> 00:58:09.110
And so they told the other cast members that they could leave for the day, but the only
所以他们告诉其他演员可以先收工了，但离开船的唯一

1537
00:58:09.110 --> 00:58:12.690
way to get off the boat, because we weren't going to take the boat back and dock it.
方式，因为我们不会把船开回去靠岸。

1538
00:58:12.790 --> 00:58:16.810
No, there were these little dinghies that would pull up and you would get in the little
不，当时有那种小橡皮艇会靠过来，你得坐进那艘

1539
00:58:16.810 --> 00:58:18.070
boat and it would take you to shore.
小船里，它会把你送到岸上。

1540
00:58:18.210 --> 00:58:18.610
Exactly.
没错。

1541
00:58:19.730 --> 00:58:21.530
Well, that did not go as planned.
结果，事情并没有按计划进行。

1542
00:58:21.910 --> 00:58:22.970
No, it didn't.
确实没有。

1543
00:58:23.070 --> 00:58:25.950
I remember getting this panicky radio thing.
我记得当时收到了一个惊慌失措的无线电消息。

1544
00:58:26.450 --> 00:58:28.690
The boat with Phyllis on it is gone.
载着菲利斯的船不见了。

1545
00:58:29.030 --> 00:58:30.670
Look, look, look at my card.
看，看，看我的卡片。

1546
00:58:30.830 --> 00:58:31.650
You were on the boat too.
你当时也在那艘船上。

1547
00:58:31.650 --> 00:58:33.130
I was stranded on the boat.
我被困在那艘船上了。

1548
00:58:33.190 --> 00:58:34.990
Yeah, and Brian too, right?
对，还有布莱恩，对吧？

1549
00:58:35.090 --> 00:58:35.850
And rain.
还有雷恩。

1550
00:58:36.090 --> 00:58:37.670
And I wrote about it in my journal.
我还在日记里写过这件事。

1551
00:58:37.670 --> 00:58:39.670
Yeah, it was crazy.
没错，那太疯狂了。

1552
00:58:39.830 --> 00:58:42.630
Well, for some reason, it fixated on me that it was Phyllis.
嗯，不知为何，我当时认定那个人是菲利斯。

1553
00:58:42.790 --> 00:58:45.030
That Phyllis was, that we had lost Phyllis.
认定是菲利斯，认定我们把菲利斯弄丢了。

1554
00:58:45.030 --> 00:58:47.850
She seems like the most vulnerable of the group, right?
她看起来是这群人里最脆弱的一个，对吧？

1555
00:58:48.030 --> 00:58:48.830
Kind Phyllis.
善良的菲利斯。

1556
00:58:48.910 --> 00:58:49.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1557
00:58:49.370 --> 00:58:52.410
So I wrote her about it and she-
所以我写信问了她，然后她——

1558
00:58:52.410 --> 00:58:53.510
I can't wait to hear what she says.
我迫不及待想听听她怎么说。

1559
00:58:53.510 --> 00:58:57.890
Yeah, well, she says the first memory, she said it was about 2.30 in the morning and
嗯，她说第一个记忆，她说当时大约是凌晨两点半，

1560
00:58:57.890 --> 00:59:00.550
she was waiting to leave the ship.
她正等着离开那艘船。

1561
00:59:00.770 --> 00:59:05.810
And her first memory was seeing Steve Carell on a tiny little boat holding onto some kind
她最初的记忆是看到史蒂夫·卡瑞尔坐在一艘小船上，手里抓着某种

